# recording a pattern: REC arms; the first key starts the transport and records; REC again ends the take;
# PLAY plays it back at its steps. Then the Steps page (a key writes at the cursor), SEQ + EDIT undoes.
# (params: 36 Tempo 49 Quantize; events: stepS is the note at step S, in cents, or the hit)
wav record.wav
wait 300
# the Tempo page (SEQ: Groove, Pattern, Steps, Tempo, Song): 120 BPM, a sixteenth 125 ms, the bar 2 s
tap SEQ
tap SEQ
tap SEQ
tap SEQ
expect view 15
spin K1 36
expect par36 120
shot tempo.png
tap REC
expect armed 1
expect run 0
leds
# D3 starts it: step 1; A3 a quarter later (step 5); a ding slap (black 5) at the bar's half (step 9)
tapkey w8
expect run 1
expect rec 1
wait 410
tapkey w9
wait 410
shot recording.png
tapkey b4
wait 500
tap REC
expect armed 0
expect run 1
expect patev0 3
expect step0 5000
expect step4 5700
expect step8 4
# the take, played back while the transport runs: the loop starts over at 2 s
wait 450
expect outlast 5000
wait 500
expect outlast 5700
expect note5700 >5
wait 500
expect outlast 4
tap PLAY
expect run 0
# from the start: each note at its step
tap PLAY
expect run 1
wait 30
expect outlast 5000
wait 470
expect outlast 5700
tap PLAY
# armed while playing: it waits for the pattern's start (WAIT), then records loop after loop
tap PLAY
tap REC
expect wait 1
shot wait.png
wait 2000
expect rec 1
tapkey w10
wait 300
tap PLAY
expect armed 0
expect patev0 4
# SEQ + EDIT: the last take undone
press SEQ
tap EDIT
release SEQ
expect view 15
expect patev0 3
# Steps (stopped): K1 the cursor; a key writes there and moves it on; K2 the note at the cursor
tap SEQ
tap SEQ
tap SEQ
tap SEQ
expect view 14
spin K1 1
tapkey w5
expect step1 6200
spin K2 1
expect step2 5000
spin K2 -1
expect step2 -1
spin K1 -1
expect steplen1 96
spin K3 2
expect steplen1 288
wait 1500
shot steps.png
wavstop
expect dropped 0
